# Two values of one type are two: `combine(left, right)` takes two Tables by their names, from its start, and hands
# both to `join`; `join` makes a third, which no name holds, and hands it straight to `show`.

route merge.combine
step combine/join
step combine/join/Table()
step combine/show

line entry > combine call
line Table·left > combine value
line Table·right > combine value
line Table·left > combine/join/Table() value              # join's call is handed both; Table() in it reads them
line Table·right > combine/join/Table() value
line combine/join/Table() > Table@combine/join/Table() value
line Table@combine/join/Table() > combine/join value
line combine/join > Table@combine/join value
line Table@combine/join > combine/show value
line combine/show > Screen own

home Table·left combine
home Table·right combine
home Table@combine/join/Table() combine/join
home Table@combine/join combine

side entry left
side Screen right
